mimic-llm bundles one file it did not write:

  lib/mimic/agent/codex_fallback_prompt.md

It is a verbatim copy of the Codex CLI system prompt, taken from
unslothai/unsloth (unsloth_cli/codex_fallback_prompt.md), which in turn carries
it from OpenAI's Codex CLI. Both projects are licensed under the Apache License
2.0:

  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

The file is unmodified. `Mimic::Agent::Codex` reads it as the `base_instructions`
of the model catalog entry it writes for Codex, because a local llama.cpp server
has no hosted backend to supply them.

